    "https://secure.entertimeonline.com/ta/ColbySawyer.careers?ShowJob=537238016": {
      "title": "ColbySawyer:Career Search",
      "description": "ColbySawyer:Career Search Skip to Main Content Log in Director of Facilities Show All Jobs Apply Show Map Location 541 Main Street,\n    \n                      New London, NH, 03257,\n                      United States Employee Type Exempt FT Manage Others Yes Minimum Experience 5 Years Contact information Name Human Resources Phone 603.526.3704 Email cscjobs@colby-sawyer.edu Description Provide leadership, direction, and oversight of all facilities operations across the college’s campus, totaling approximately 650,000 square feet, ensuring a safe, functional and welcoming campus environment. Responsible for management of building maintenance services, grounds including snow removal, college fleet operations, preventative maintenance, events support, environmental services and other duties as assigned. Manage and oversee building construction, campus renovations projects and campus initiatives that supports the strategic goals of the institution. Works collaboratively with all constituents of the college to support departmental and college objectives. This position develops and implements strategic facilities plans that are aligned with institutional priorities, ensures regulatory compliance, oversees departmental budgets, and fosters a culture of safety, customer service, operational excellence, and continuous improvement. The director serves as the primary facilities liaison with campus departments, public agencies and external vendors. Essential Job Functions 1. Provide overall leadership and direction for Facilities Management operations including maintenance, grounds, snow/ice removal, fleet management, event support, and environmental services 2. Develop and implement short- and long-term facilities plans that align with the college’s strategic goals 3. Develop and manage deferred maintenance plan and annually evaluate for equipment and buildings 4. Advise senior leadership on facilities planning, infrastructure needs, and capital priorities 5. Ensure timely and effective facility set-ups for academic programs and campus events 6. Develop and manage departmental operating budget; monitor expenses to ensure fiscal responsibility; oversee procurement processes, bid documents, vendor selection and contract management 7. Provide leadership in recruitment, performance evaluation, and professional development 8. Promote a culture of safety, collaboration, accountability and customer service excellence 9. Ensure staff training in regulatory compliance, safety standards and best practices 10. Ensure compliance with all applicable local, state, and federal regulations (OSHA, ADA, environmental regulations and EEO requirements) 11. Maintain appropriate documentation, inspections, certifications and reporting requirements 12. Provide assistance during campus emergencies, severe weather events and after-hours incidents, ensuring continuity of operations planning for facilities-related functions 13. Occasional evening and weekend work is required, along with on-call duties Requirements Required Qualifications 1. Bachelor’s degree or equivalent combination of education and experience in facilities management, engineering, business administration, operations, or a related field 2. Minimum of 5-7 years of progressively responsible facilities management experience, including supervisory and budget oversight experience 3. Able to communicate effectively both orally and in writing 4. Strong organizational, communication, and interpersonal skills 5. Ability to establish and maintain positive working relationships in a diverse environment 6. Working knowledge of building, electrical, plumbing, and HVAC systems 7. Valid driver’s license Preferred Qualifications 1. Experience in higher education facilities management 2. Knowledge of New Hampshire contracting and building processes 3. Professional certification such as Certified Facility Manager (CFM), Certified Educational Facilities Professional (CEFP), or equivalent Physical Requirements The essential functions of this job require an individual who is able to adequately (1) communicate with all members of the facilities team and senior leadership of the college, (2) be proficient in computer literacy including spreadsheets, word processing, database processing and project management tools, In the course of the typical workday, one may be required to transport oneself short distances to the core campus to attend campus meetings and events and to assess campus-wide facility concerns. Summary Colby-Sawyer College is a comprehensive liberal arts-based institution located in the scenic Lake Sunapee area of New Hampshire. We have friendly people, beautiful nature, and small-town amenities and shops. We are located about 35 minutes south of Dartmouth College and just 1 hour 30 minutes from Boston. For more information see Lake Sunapee Region Chamber of Commerce, NH . We strive to always be a people-first organization. We are passionate about building and sustaining an inclusive and equitable working environment for all employees. If you are looking for a place where you will feel welcome and that you belong, Colby-Sawyer College is that place. Colby-Sawyer is especially interested in candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of the institution. Applicants are encouraged to share what they can offer and how they can help us to achieve and maintain these values in their cover letter. Interested candidates may also visit Human Resources in Colgate Hall Room 230, Monday through Friday from 8am - 5pm, to alternatively complete a paper application. Review of candidates will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Colby-Sawyer College is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We are committed to maintaining a diverse workforce and an inclusive work environment which celebrates multiple perspectives. Colby-Sawyer College will not tolerate discrimination in employment or employment-related decisions on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, national origin, gender, religion, age, mental or physical disability, family or marital status, sexual orientation, veteran status, genetic information, or gender identity."
    },
    "https://secure.entertimeonline.com/ta/ColbySawyer.careers?ShowJob=537226260": {
      "title": "ColbySawyer:Career Search",
      "description": "ColbySawyer:Career Search Skip to Main Content Log in Men's & Women's Indoor-Outdoor Track & Field - Throws Show All Jobs Apply Show Map Location 541 Main Street,\n    \n                      New London, NH, 03257,\n                      United States Employee Type Exempt PT > 20 hours Required Degree NONE Contact information Name Human Resources Phone 603.526.3704 Email CSCjobs@colby-sawyer.edu Description Colby-Sawyer College seeks an Assistant Coach to assist with the activities of the Men's and Women's Indoor-Outdoor Track & Field team, participate in the growth and development of every student athlete, promote healthy lifestyles and interpersonal skills. The Assistant may periodically be asked to assume overall responsibility in the absence of the Head Coach. Responsibilities Perform key program implementation functions for assign team, in conjunction with the mission and culture of the college and in consultation with the Head Coach. Serve as professional educator for student athletes, primarily with the throwing events, encouraging individual as well as team goal setting, acknowledging individual challenges and achievements, encouraging academic achievement and positive social interactions at all times. Carry out specific team development tasks as assigned. May include: generating on-campus participants, conditioning of athletes, monitoring academic and personal development through program evaluations. Plan and carry out team practice sessions, coach team during games, modeling good sportsmanship and positive social interactions at all times. Assist in the recruitment of student athletes: maintain up-to-date files of prospective students; evaluate athletic performance and potential; meet with prospective students; participate in special department recruitment programs/activities. Participate in various athletic advertising and fundraising efforts. Maintain strict compliance with all college, conference and NCAA rules and regulations. Requirements Certifications appropriate to the relevant sport, division, or other regulating agency. High school or college coaching experience, with collegiate playing experience desirable, or a combination of education and experience from which comparable knowledge and skills are acquired. Basic knowledge and skills related to college athletic programs, with demonstrated skills in track & field throwing events. Demonstrated basic teaching/coaching skills. Demeanor to deal effectively with students, parents, coaches and other college athletics personnel, and other CSC personnel in carrying out the recruitment and coaching aspects of the job . Physical Requirements The essential functions of this job require an individual who is able to adequately (1) communicate well enough to be understood by others, (2) operate a personal computer and (3) use a telephone. In the course of the typical workday, one may be required to transport oneself short distances in order to attend campus meetings and events. These distances will generally not exceed three standard city blocks. Summary Colby-Sawyer College is a comprehensive liberal arts-based institution located in the scenic Lake Sunapee area of New Hampshire. We have friendly people, beautiful nature, and small-town amenities and shops. We are located about 35 minutes south of Dartmouth College and just 1 hour 30 minutes from Boston. For more information see Lake Sunapee Region Chamber of Commerce, NH . We strive to always be a people-first organization. We are passionate about building and sustaining an inclusive and equitable working environment for all employees. If you are looking for a place where you will feel welcome and that you belong, Colby-Sawyer College is that place. Colby-Sawyer is especially interested in candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of the institution. Applicants are encouraged to share what they can offer and how they can help us to achieve and maintain these values in their cover letter. Interested candidates may also visit Human Resources in Colgate Hall Room 230, Monday through Friday from 8am - 5pm, to alternatively complete a paper application. Review of candidates will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Colby-Sawyer College is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We are committed to maintaining a diverse workforce and an inclusive work environment which celebrates multiple perspectives. Colby-Sawyer College will not tolerate discrimination in employment or employment-related decisions on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, national origin, gender, religion, age, mental or physical disability, family or marital status, sexual orientation, veteran status, genetic information, or gender identity."
    },
